  biomeName: Coral-Porous Walls
  minDepthMeters: 300
  maxDepthMeters: 600
  shortDescription: Ancient fossilized reef walls honeycombed with holes and micro-caverns.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather basics,
    and keep orientation in soft terrain and hunt hidden value.
  commonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Fiber Kelp and Membrane Tissue.
  rareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Biolum Paste and Fiber Mesh.'
  landmarkIdentity: Coral-Porous Walls reads through dunes, plains, void cuts, and
    shape changes in the floor. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are frequent. The player should often see a clear
    reset point nearby.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: orientation loss and long empty recovery swims.
    Creature pressure stays medium.'
  extractionFocus: 'Mixed salvage, harvest pockets, and risky reef-node peels. Early
    tier: keep runs short and accept longer sweeps and weaker orientation during
    gathering.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is reef crown or porous fossil wall. This slot
    should read through coral windows and rib-like skeletons; use silhouette changes
    to avoid getting lost in soft terrain.
